<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="chapter_3" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Quadratic Functions</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
        Describing the path of a projectile, designing lenses to bend and focus light, and maximizing revenue in certain business situations are just a few of the places that <em>quadratic functions</em> can be utilized. With <q>U</q>-shaped graphs known as parabolas, these functions allow us to model and understand a remarkable array of real-world phenomena.
    </p>
</introduction>

